  "title": "Energy in an Inductor: Why It's One Half L I Squared",
  "eyebrow": "energy and power",
  "language": "en",
  "duration": 49,
  "topic": "Energy stored in an inductor — ramping current builds a magnetic field; the work integral ∫v·i dt collapses to ½LI² via Φ = L·I, giving the three equivalent forms ½LI², ½ΦI, and Φ²/(2L)",
